{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447763-limiting-trinkets","id":1447763,"title":"Limiting Trinkets?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-06T22:04:59-07:00","id":1447763,"title":"Limiting Trinkets?","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> I'm new to Mage (as a storyteller) and I'm a little bit worried about the &quot;projected availability&quot; of trinkets (among my players). Trinkets are pretty easy to make: necessary sphere(s) plus 10 successes (ritual) and voila...you coat now is bulletproof.<br /> <br /> What stops a Mage from making a trinket out of every piece of cloth or tool she wears or uses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T01:57:51-07:00","id":1447780,"title":"","content":"Hi, <br /> <br /> Isn't it paradox, when walking around like a whole umbrareign?<br /> Additionally, everybody will find you, even he was looking for someone else, because of all your magic signature.<br /> But well, I guess, those are no &quot;Hard rules&quot; and you could go all powermage with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26522-quin_shihuangdi","name":"Quin_Shihuangdi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T02:54:43-07:00","id":1447784,"title":"","content":"The main limiting factor? Why bother?<br /> <br /> It's not like making your undershirt, shirt, and coat lets you get 24 Armor or something. Basically, these things don't stack in a meaningful way, so the only point to turning everything into a Trinket would be to have a lot of backup options for what you think you're going to need that day.<br /> <br /> If you get too restrictive about these things, you're reducing the main fun of tech-mage gadget types like a lot of Etherites that tend to use a lot of Trinkets and tools because their Focus is more restrictive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T04:57:49-07:00","id":1447793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447763-limiting-trinkets#post1447763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> I'm new to Mage (as a storyteller) and I'm a little bit worried about the &quot;projected availability&quot; of trinkets (among my players). Trinkets are pretty easy to make: necessary sphere(s) plus 10 successes (ritual) and voila...you coat now is bulletproof.<br /> <br /> What stops a Mage from making a trinket out of every piece of cloth or tool she wears or uses?</div> </div> </div> </div>My advice, don't look at this issue as a problem. Instead, look at what it means for the character and the story. The character is spending a lot of time making these things. How much? Who notices? What does it mean for their reputation? What does it mean for their opportunities? Who does it irritate? Who does it impress?<br /> <br /> Use the answers to connect the characters into the world and the world into the characters. <br /> <br /> Sure, if down the line you find that it is destroying game balance, address it then. In general, though, the benefits of the players engaging with the game and the world outweighs potential system issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:58:31-07:00","id":1447801,"title":"","content":"Btw, just to clarify this, once trinkets are made, do they generate paradox every time they display their magical effects? (supposing those magical effects are vulgar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:14:23-07:00","id":1447803,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that \u201cTrinket\u201d is basically a fancy term for \u201can object that has had a permanent Effect placed on it\u201d. There are no special rules for them, other than some rough guidelines for assigning Background ratings to them. <br /> <br /> To Argonaut's question, the answer is that you generate the Paradox when you place the Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2021, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T09:32:53-07:00","id":1447823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447763-limiting-trinkets?p=1447803#post1447803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that \u201cTrinket\u201d is basically a fancy term for \u201can object that has had a permanent Effect placed on it\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> Indeed.<br /> <br /> It's not really worse, in terms of an exploit, than any regular buff that can be alowed into permanency, or lasting six months (and then re-cast). Prob. should be ruled just like those.<br /> <br /> In terms of Paradox: I think something can be said bout too Vulgar Effects not being granted permanency. Or not w/o Permadox, weird flaws, or other kind of consequences. Trinkets tend to be subtle stuff. Don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T09:38:51-07:00","id":1447824,"title":"","content":"On that note, I would also point out that there are effects that would be vulgar normally that are considered coincidental if I Wonder is involved. For this purpose only, I would consider a Trinket to be a kind of Wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T10:11:30-07:00","id":1447829,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that's more common sense than a strict rule (albeit it's presented as one). Like, a sword on fire it's more believable than a sword <i>of </i>fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T14:00:08-07:00","id":1447842,"title":"","content":"Unbelief, while frustratingly still lacking in good guidelines/mechanics, is the form of Paradox that concerns Trinkets: if they do something that becomes Vulgar, the magic in them would start to unravel. It might not be flashy or nasty like normal Paradox, but mages that aren't careful with making sure their Trinkets are adequately disguised to Consensus could easily find them failing at the exact worst time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T18:12:14-07:00","id":1448179,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops a PC from creating a bunch of Trinkets. Nor should the ST deny them simply because of abstract fears of &quot;game balance&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of in-universe reasons why it might not be the best idea.<br /> <br /> For one, permanent Effects radiate Prime auras to those people or things able to sense magick. There are ways to disguise such things, of course - it's assumed that the heavily enchanted Chantries of the Traditions are shielded against Technocratic Prime sensors - but on their own such permanent Effects are neon signs reading &quot;Magic User here!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the Technocracy, you have witch hunters, some of whom may have dots in Awareness sufficient to notice the Mage's running Effects. Even if they only have a feeling, and not any concrete idea about what the Mage is or what it means. Witch hunters with that much Awareness learn to trust their instincts. If nothing else, it'll encourage the hunter to investigate the PC further.<br /> <br /> Another factor: Bygones. Rogue magickal creatures in the material world are constantly on the prowl for sources of Quintessence, to sustain themselves in a Reality that hates them. Whether a Bygone can eat a Mage's enchanted shirt and gain Quintessence from it is immaterial. Just the fact that it reeks of life-giving magick is enough to set a mana-starved beast into attack mode. Or to encourage smaller Bygones to follow the PC, find where they live, and burrow into their closet to snack on their wardrobe. Imagine a cloud of Bygone moths, gnawing holes in the PC's clothes while they're out adventuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":".  Spelling Error 05-15-2021, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T20:10:14-07:00","id":1448563,"title":"","content":"I understand Trinkets to basically just be the &quot;Quick and Dirty Artifacts&quot; from <i>Forged by Dragons </i>fire. I can see some of these things actively radiating magical energy, but by that same token, some of the most useful items there don't create an active effect so much as they appear to simply have had their actual material composition changed in some way. For instance, the most used one of these things among my players is the spider silk. You turn cotton to spider silk, and any such garment basically does damage conversion: Agg becomes Lethal, and Lethal becomes Bashing. I don't know that that's necessarily actively radiating an prime magic or displays on ongoing effect, though a cursory magical inspection would reveal its likely magical origin; and scanning with Matter will obviously reveal it's nature. I also don't think it's terribly overpowered--Mages are squishy enough that walking around with lightly armored clothes (even +3 to +4 with no dex penalty), damage conversion, quiet sneakers, a very light backpack, accurized firearms or very sharp blades, what-have-you, is not going to give them some crazy edge over other mages since none of these things are unanswerable end-all-be-all capabilties, and they're not necessarily exclusive to any given faction; so it just becomes a new set of bells and whistles in the magical arms race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}